# Paths an agent may change but not merge on its own. The main ruleset requires a code
# owner's approval for any PR that touches them; every other path auto-merges once CI
# is green. GitHub reads this file from the base branch, so a PR cannot loosen it for
# itself. Policy and reasoning: .claude/rules/pull-requests.md → Auto-merge.

# On-device data: a bad migration or store change can lose someone's library.
/SilverScreen/Data/Persistence/        @collinbrowse

# What the app declares to Apple and asks the OS for.
/SilverScreen/Info.plist               @collinbrowse
/SilverScreen/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy    @collinbrowse
*.entitlements                         @collinbrowse

# Versions, release tooling, and signing.
/Version.xcconfig                      @collinbrowse
/Config.xcconfig                       @collinbrowse
/scripts/release.py                    @collinbrowse
/scripts/asc_api.py                    @collinbrowse
/scripts/asc_media.py                  @collinbrowse

# The TMDB proxy, which holds the token and serves every request.
/worker/                               @collinbrowse

# The harness itself: CI, hooks, rules, validators, and this file.
/.github/                              @collinbrowse
/.claude/                              @collinbrowse
/CLAUDE.md                             @collinbrowse
/scripts/validate-*.py                 @collinbrowse
/scripts/test_claude_hooks.py          @collinbrowse
